[I] Xfce configuration daemon and utilities

[T] Xfconf is the configuration storage system of Xfce, a hierarchical tree
[T] whose root children are called channels and whose settings beneath them
[T] are called properties. Applications access it through a D-Bus daemon and
[T] client library.

[U] https://www.xfce.org/

[A] Olivier Fourdan <fourdan@xfce.org>
[A] Jasper Huijsmans <jasper@moongroup.com>
[A] Benedikt Meurer <benedikt.meurer@unix-ag.uni-siegen.de>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/desktop/xfce
[F] CROSS NO-LTO.clang

[L] LGPL
[V] 4.20.0

[P] X -----5---9 222.400

[D] 9c53cfad31ee73450cae2bb2e5d60655eaf48b898dcb8355994f376a xfconf-4.20.0.tar.bz2 https://archive.xfce.org/src/xfce/xfconf/4.20/

. $base/package/xfce4/*/xfce4-conf.in

var_append makeopt ' ' systemd_userdir=/usr/lib/systemd/user
var_append makeopt ' ' servicedir=/usr/share/dbus-1/services
makeinstopt="$makeopt"' DESTDIR="$root" install'
